# Copy to .env and edit. Read by app/dashboard.py and scripts/*.sh; the real environment
# wins over this file. Never commit .env (it is git-ignored).
# Paths may start with ~ or $HOME.

# --- data (two PRIVATE git repos; scripts/init-data-repos.sh creates them)
# Local clone of your task vault (task lists, project metadata, inbox).
ASSISTANT_VAULT=$HOME/assistant/vault
# Local clone of your progress-notes repo. Default: a "notes" folder next to the vault.
ASSISTANT_NOTES=$HOME/assistant/notes

# --- categories: top-level task folders, in display order, as folder:Label.
# folder = tasks/<folder>/ in the vault; Label = the chip / filter / [Label] tag text.
# Use one-word labels (they also become CSS class names). Up to 6 get distinct colours.
CATEGORIES=work:Work,side:Side,life:Life
# Category preselected in "Add a task" rows that let you pick one (default: the last).
DEFAULT_CATEGORY=Life

# --- dashboard
# Page title.
DASHBOARD_BRAND=Tasks
# Port on 127.0.0.1 (the dashboard never listens on other interfaces).
DASHBOARD_PORT=8765
# Where the generated cache (data.json, stubs.json) goes. Default: <vault>/dashboard
# DASHBOARD_CACHE=$HOME/assistant/vault/dashboard
# scripts/open-dashboard.sh fast-forwards this kit checkout to origin/main on each launch
# (only when it is on main with no local edits). Set to 1 to turn that off.
DASHBOARD_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=0
# Seconds the launcher waits for that fetch.
# DASHBOARD_UPDATE_TIMEOUT=5
# Path of this kit checkout (normally detected; set it if you run the scripts from elsewhere).
# ASSISTANT_INFRA=$HOME/task-dashboard-kit

# --- GitHub (optional): project cards show commits / PRs / code TODO files of the repos
# listed in memory/projects/*.md. The dashboard calls the GitHub CLI `gh`, which uses its
# own login (`gh auth login`) or GH_TOKEN. Minimal fine-grained token: read-only
# "Contents" + "Metadata" + "Pull requests" on the code repos you link; add write
# "Contents" only if you want to close code TODOs from the dashboard.
# GH_TOKEN=

# --- link-notes bookkeeping (machine-specific map of project → code folder)
# ASSISTANT_CONFIG_DIR=$HOME/.config/assistant

# --- Windows shortcuts (scripts/install-windows-shortcuts.sh, WSL only)
# DASHBOARD_SHORTCUT_NAME=Tasks
# DASHBOARD_ICON_LOCATION=
